       41  '''Ocnița''' ({{IPAc-ro|lang|pron|'|O|c|n|i|ț|a}}) is a district ({{Langx|ro|[[raion]]}}) in the north of [[Moldova]], with the administrative center at [[Ocnița]]. The other major cities are [[Otaci]] and [[Frunză, Ocnița|Frunză]]. As of the [[2024 Moldovan census]], its population was 31,610.
       42  ==History==
       43  The first evidence of a locality in the district comes from 1419, when is attested the city [[Otaci]], called Stânca Vămii. Other historical attestations of district towns down to the period 1422–1431 when the localities are listed first: [[Hădărăuți]], [[Mihălășeni, Ocnița|Mihălășeni]], [[Lipnic]],
       44  ==Geography==
